- Drafted `/tmp/lobu-mcp-agent-discovery-handoff.md` as a standalone brief.
- Included: mission, executive verdict, clean-room prompt matrix, observed production ground truth, evaluation rubric, error-message corpus, likely root causes, recommended implementation order, anti-slop constraints, test plan, merge gates, and definition of done.
- Kept the handoff out of the repo and verified it existed and had substantial content (828 lines).

Failures and how to do differently:

- The first attempt at the handoff needed integrity checks to ensure the file was complete and not truncated; future agents should verify the path, line count, and opening/closing sections immediately after writing.
- The audit uncovered a separate Gemini/Antigravity toolchain blocker while trying to run clean-room comparisons; future similar work should keep that environment issue segregated from the Lobu deliverable.

